    "body": "# fix(lsp): advance inline completion range over matching input\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n`Completor:accept()` applies the item against the range the server answered\r\nwith. Characters typed after the request but before accepting lie inside\r\nneither that range nor the replacement, so they survive the insertion: typing\r\n`a` after `foob` and accepting `foobar` within the 200 ms debounce yields\r\n`foobara`.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nGrow the item's range over the characters typed since the request, so that\r\n`accept()` replaces them. Only while the candidate still matches, decided by\r\nthe longest common prefix `show()` already computes, so input that contradicts\r\nit is left alone. Snippet items are unaffected: `accept()` only honours the\r\nrange for plain text.\r\n\r\nTest: `get() does not leave behind text typed since the request`.\r\n\r\nFixes #36529\r\n\r\nAI-ssisted\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-24T14:51:40Z",
